WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:09.500
Alphabet, Google’s parent company and owner
of the YouTube platform, is negotiating to

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:13.390
build a technology center in none other than
Saudi Arabia.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:14.760
Sounds incredible...

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.890
but the truth is that since Mohammed Bin Salman,
the Crown Prince, took over, this country

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.760
has changed a lot...

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.349
at least much more than anyone would’ve
imagined a few years ago.

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:37.390
So, my friends, let's take a look at what’s
happening in Saudi Arabia.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.449
To understand what’s happening in Saudi
Arabia, we need to take a look at their past,

00:00:41.449 --> 00:00:42.990
to see where everything began.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:47.429
Well, first of all, we need to bear in mind
that we’re talking about a particularly

00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:48.780
young country...

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.410
Saudi Arabia was formally born in 1932.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:56.179
Then, of course, Saudi Arabia was very different
to what it is today.

00:00:56.179 --> 00:01:00.140
See, back then, its many oil deposits hadn’t
been discovered yet, so it was a very poor

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:06.730
place that still had a sparse, semi nomadic
population.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:10.350
Basically…

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.430
Saudi Arabia was still in the Middle Ages...

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:18.310
Well, now that I think about it, a lot of
things haven’t changed much.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:23.260
But... a few years later, in 1938, the first
oil deposits were discovered... and since

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.260
then...

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:28.220
Well let's say that Saud House, the country’s
royal house, has used oil money to make Arabia

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:33.750
look like the United States, at least in terms
of aesthetics and leisure.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:38.570
Allow me to explain myself.

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:43.100
We’re talking, for example, of cities inspired
by Dallas, driving American cars and building

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.160
huge malls in the middle of the desert.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:48.850
And that’s exactly what they did for decades.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:54.090
But... not only that, over the years, the
Saudi government, who, thanks to oil, had

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:58.820
begun to have a lot of money, came to a kind
of agreement with Washington that has lasted,

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.870
more or less, until today.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:01.870
Check out this agreement:

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:06.210
Saudi Arabia guarantees a huge and relatively
cheap oil supply, using the dollar as its

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.660
basic currency – have you heard of petrodollars?

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:13.660
- and accumulates all the money it generates
in oil sales in US treasury debt or in the

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.530
big Wall Street banks.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:20.190
And if that weren’t enough, the Saudi government
is always willing to inject millions into

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:27.810
the powerful US arms industry.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.310
That is, lots of oil, lots of money, and great
business for the US military industry.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:37.140
The question is, in exchange for what?

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:43.200
Well, my friends, basically for protection.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.610
The Saud house bought what essentially amounts
to insurance from Washington to protect it

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.280
from foreign enemies.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.319
However, in 1979... everything changed.

00:02:52.319 --> 00:02:58.500
See, this year, 1979, was a fundamental year
for Arabia and for Islam.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.670
On the one hand, the Islamic Khomeini revolution
happened in Iran; on the other, the Soviet

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:07.810
Union invaded Afghanistan, and in Saudi Arabia,
between November 20th and December 4th, a

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.980
group of fanatics took over the great Mosque
of Mecca and accused the Saud House, the Saudi

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:17.130
monarchy, of betraying Islam and selling their
soul to the West.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.540
Fanatics called for an uprising to overthrow
the royal family.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.590
And there, dear viewers, is where everything
changed.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:28.770
The Saud House leaders feared a revolutionary
uprising and decided to please the extremists.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.430
The United States could protect them from
a foreign enemy, but it would be very hard

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:37.870
for them to do so in a popular uprising like
the one that happened that year in Iran.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:45.430
So, even though Arabia wasn’t precisely
a paradise of freedom, from that moment on,

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:49.060
things got a lot, lot worse:

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:54.160
Discrimination against women reached stratospheric
levels, the religious guard began an uncontrolled

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.050
campaign and Saudi Arabia began to finance
all kinds of extremist groups like there were

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:03.240
no tomorrow... both inside and outside the
country.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.540
And that’s precisely the Saudi Arabia we
all know.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.540
However...

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:11.319
just a moment, because there was another turning
point in 2015.

00:04:11.319 --> 00:04:15.930
This time thanks to plummeting oil prices
and the arrival of a new king, Salman bin

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:20.579
Abdulaziz.

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:29.710
A king, dear viewers, who decided to give
almost all the power to his son and now heir,

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:33.720
Mohammed Bin Salman, of whom we already talked
about here, on VISUALPOLITIK.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.620
Thus, a new generation took hold of the country.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.960
(“My generation was held hostage by 1979.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.830
I know now that my kids will not be hostages”.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:43.569
One Saudi banker to New York Times.)

00:04:43.569 --> 00:04:51.789
Since then, folks, a new kind of revolution
has been launched to modernize the country.

00:04:51.789 --> 00:04:55.580
We've already talked about this on this channel,
but the truth is that the plan is advancing

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.460
at full speed based on 3 pillars:

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.199
The fight against corruption, economic change
and religious reform.

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:13.470
So, without further ado, let's see what’s
happening, point by point.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:24.509
(THE FIGHT AGAINST CORRUPTION)

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:29.610
The crown prince has said it both actively
and passively, corruption in Saudi Arabia

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.500
is a great burden and has to end.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:36.580
( “Our country has suffered a lot from corruption
from the 1980s until today.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:39.870
The calculation of our experts is that roughly
10 percent of all government spending was

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:43.249
siphoned off by corruption each year, from
the top levels to the bottom”.

00:05:43.249 --> 00:05:44.529
Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman)

00:05:44.529 --> 00:05:45.999
And you know what?

00:05:45.999 --> 00:05:46.999
It wasn’t only said.

00:05:46.999 --> 00:05:47.999
It was done.

00:05:47.999 --> 00:05:52.810
Last November 2017: princes, businessmen,
ministers, ex-politicians… a huge number

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:56.280
of people were invited to dine with the king
or to meet with the crown prince.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.949
And they were all arrested and detained.

00:05:57.949 --> 00:06:01.689
Of course, in a prison we would only see in
a country like this:

00:06:01.689 --> 00:06:06.979
The Ritz-Carlton Riyadh, a very, very luxurious
hotel.

00:06:06.979 --> 00:06:07.979
Of course...

00:06:07.979 --> 00:06:09.189
not everything was comfortable...

00:06:09.189 --> 00:06:13.419
after all, it became a prison that held such
illustrious prisoners as Prince Alwaleed Bin

00:06:13.419 --> 00:06:18.499
Talal, grandson of the kingdom’s own founder,
known as the Warren Buffet of the Middle East.

00:06:18.499 --> 00:06:22.469
A prince who according to Forbes magazine’s
calculations, has a fortune of almost 18 billion

00:06:22.469 --> 00:06:25.979
dollars and is one of Twitter’s largest
shareholders.

00:06:25.979 --> 00:06:29.449
Well... not even he managed to escape.

00:06:29.449 --> 00:06:34.409
All prisoners were held incommunicado and
couldn’t even contact their lawyers.

00:06:34.409 --> 00:06:35.409
Rights?

00:06:35.409 --> 00:06:36.409
Legal guarantees?

00:06:36.409 --> 00:06:37.529
We’re in Saudi Arabia!

00:06:37.529 --> 00:06:38.529
But...

00:06:38.529 --> 00:06:42.199
What do you think the Saudi government asked
for to release them?

00:06:42.199 --> 00:06:46.710
Well, nothing less than giving part of their
fortunes and companies as compensation for

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.499
all the corruption they were involved in.

00:06:48.499 --> 00:06:49.499
And...

00:06:49.499 --> 00:06:50.499
here’s a question.

00:06:50.499 --> 00:06:53.979
Do you know how much the Saudi government
raised with this trick?

00:06:53.979 --> 00:06:56.199
Listen up, because this is an astounding number:

00:06:56.199 --> 00:07:03.210
It wasn’t 1, nor 5, nor 10 billion but approximately
an eye-popping 107 billion dollars.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:06.620
You heard that right!

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:12.110
Of course, a few detractors have accused the
crown prince of carrying out this campaign

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:16.749
not with the intention of fighting corruption
but with the aim of strengthening his power

00:07:16.749 --> 00:07:20.129
and, for example, seizing control of foreign-based
media.

00:07:20.129 --> 00:07:23.259
Yes, the detainees included important media
businessmen.

00:07:23.259 --> 00:07:33.240
But my friends, this doesn’t end here, not
at all.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:38.419
(THE ECONOMIC CHANGE)

00:07:38.419 --> 00:07:44.369
As we mentioned on VISUALPOLITIK, Saudi Arabia
wants to emulate Dubai and leave their oil

00:07:44.369 --> 00:07:45.369
dependence behind.

00:07:45.369 --> 00:07:47.789
And they want to do it hand in hand with private
capital.

00:07:47.789 --> 00:07:52.169
Just as we saw in Google’s case.

00:07:52.169 --> 00:07:56.999
Of course... on the other hand, Prince Mohammed
Bin Salman is also very fond of big Pharaonic

00:07:56.999 --> 00:07:57.999
projects.

00:07:57.999 --> 00:08:03.139
The last one he publicized was NEOM, a macro-city
that the Riyadh government wants to build

00:08:03.139 --> 00:08:07.460
in the Red Sea, next to Jordan and Egypt.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:09.639
And check out these numbers,

00:08:09.639 --> 00:08:11.869
500, 500 billion dollars!

00:08:11.869 --> 00:08:17.460
in public and private investment to urbanize
and build a city in an area that is larger

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:22.740
than El Salvador, a 10,000 square mile space
which will have its own laws, its own courts

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:24.250
and its own taxes.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:28.720
A new city that the crown prince wants to
turn into a great transport hub and a huge

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.619
international business center.

00:08:30.619 --> 00:08:35.000
So basically, a much more modern and much,
much bigger Dubai.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:38.270
And, this isn’t his only project…

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:42.000
(“Saudi Arabia Plans a Huge Red Sea Beach
Tourism Project.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:47.050
The project will cover 50 islands and 34,000
square kilometers -- an area bigger than Belgium”

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:48.050
Bloomberg)

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.050
There’s a few more.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:52.600
The prince’s idea is to get all these cities
to have laws and standards different from

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:54.389
those in the rest of the country.

00:08:54.389 --> 00:08:58.240
Laws that can attract investors, tourists
and entrepreneurs...

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:02.850
The question is: will Riyadh really be able
to make all these projects work in a country

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.680
that is so anchored in the past?

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:08.190
( “Saudi Arabia to build five royal palaces
in NEOM”.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:09.190
Arabia Watch)

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.190
With news like that...

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:13.279
it doesn’t seem easy at first, but we’ll
see.

00:09:13.279 --> 00:09:19.350
So far, people like Richard Branson support
this strategy.

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:24.880
(THE RELIGIOUS CHANGE)

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:31.240
Lastly, there’s the religious change, the
prince’s latest great obsession is the struggle

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:35.010
against Islam’s fundamentalism or its most
radical interpretations.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:40.839
See, Saudi Arabia is a country of restrictions,
I think we all know that, and it may never

00:09:40.839 --> 00:09:42.089
cease being so.

00:09:42.089 --> 00:09:46.569
However, just a few years ago nobody could’ve
imagined we’d see so many changes, and so

00:09:46.569 --> 00:09:48.509
quickly, in this country.

00:09:48.509 --> 00:09:51.000
Concerts and movies, which had been banned,
have returned to the country.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.230
The religious guard has lost almost all its
power, women can now attend sports stadiums

00:09:55.230 --> 00:10:00.440
and since June, can also drive.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:05.360
Without going any further, on December 6th,
2017, the Lebanese singer Hiba Tawaji, starred

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.329
in Saudi Arabia’s first all-woman concert
in this country..

00:10:08.329 --> 00:10:11.050
Yes, the audience was entirely made up of
women...

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:14.779
but this was a step we couldn’t have imagined
just 3 years ago.

00:10:14.779 --> 00:10:17.130
Listen to the reflection a young man from
this country shared with the NYT:

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.529
(“We are privileged to be the generation
that has seen the before and the after.”

00:10:20.529 --> 00:10:23.769
The previous generation of Saudi women, she
explained, could never imagine a day when

00:10:23.769 --> 00:10:27.819
a woman could drive and the coming generation
will never be able to imagine a day when a

00:10:27.819 --> 00:10:28.819
woman couldn’t”.

00:10:28.819 --> 00:10:31.730
A 30-year-old Saudi woman social entrepreneur
to New York Times.)

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:37.060
The person in charge of this entire process,
Mohamed Bin Salman;

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:43.810
(“We are ‘restoring’ Islam to its origins,
and our biggest tools are the Prophet’s

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:44.810
practices.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.540
At the time of the Prophet Muhammad there
were musical theaters, there was mixing between

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.770
men and women, there was respect for Christians
and Jews in Arabia.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:53.060
The first commercial judge in Medina was a
woman!

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:56.750
So if the Prophet embraced all of this, do
you mean the Prophet was not a Muslim?”

00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.029
Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman.)

00:10:58.029 --> 00:11:02.639
For a Saudi Arabian leader to say something
like that... wow.

00:11:02.639 --> 00:11:06.410
And, by the way, my friends, don’t think
that Saudi Arabia was always the place it

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:07.410
was in the past.

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:12.959
Of course, it was always a very, very conservative
country, too conservative, but not the hell

00:11:12.959 --> 00:11:14.320
it became since 1979.

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:19.610
In short, as you can see, even though there’s
still a lot to change… things seem to be

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:20.810
on the right track...

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:23.910
Although of course there are also dark areas.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.920
The Qatar blockade failure, the Yemen war,
and the prince's obsession with Tehran:

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.550
( “Iran’s supreme leader is the new Hitler
of the Middle East.

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:33.699
But we learned from Europe that appeasement
doesn’t work.

00:11:33.699 --> 00:11:37.660
We don’t want the new Hitler in Iran to
repeat what happened in Europe in the Middle

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:38.660
East.”

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:39.870
Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman.)

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:44.190
Yes, this prince is a take-charge kind of
man… but, to tell the truth, so far his

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:48.870
international attempts have been resounding
failures, as we saw with Yemen.

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.899
Another problem is that Arabia's economy is
going from bad to worse.

00:11:52.899 --> 00:11:58.880
See, in 2017, they suffered their first recession
since 2009 and public deficit is still skyrocketing,

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.389
with more than 50 billion dollars per year.

00:12:01.389 --> 00:12:05.009
And of course that can make it hard for the
prince to carry out his plans.

00:12:05.009 --> 00:12:08.370
In any case, my friends, having seen this,
I think we can say that the oil fall was some

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:12.129
of the best news for everyone, especially
for Saudi Arabian women.

00:12:12.129 --> 00:12:16.790
( "We are returning to what we were before,
a country of moderate Islam that is open to

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:18.500
all religions and to the world.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:22.079
We will not spend the next 30 years of our
lives dealing with destructive ideas.

00:12:22.079 --> 00:12:23.269
We will destroy them today.

00:12:23.269 --> 00:12:25.139
We will end extremism very soon”.

00:12:25.139 --> 00:12:26.200
Mohammed bin Salman)

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:27.529
Anyway, that's how things are.

00:12:27.529 --> 00:12:31.620
But now it’s your turn, do you think Saudi
Arabia will manage to change itself?

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:35.089
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in the survey.

00:12:35.089 --> 00:12:39.350
I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did and don’t forget to

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:42.569
subscribe to our channel for brand new videos
every Monday and Thursday.

00:12:42.569 --> 00:12:46.389
Also, don’t forget to check out our friends
at the Reconsider Media Podcast - they provided

00:12:46.389 --> 00:12:49.149
the vocals in this episode that were not mine!

00:12:49.149 --> 00:12:51.129
